# Chapter 3. Introduction to Evolutionary Computation

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:nx, "1.0.0"},
  {:kino, "0.19.1"},
  {:kino_vega_lite, "0.1.13"}
])

defmodule Chapter03.Tables do
  @moduledoc false

  @type column :: atom() | String.t()
  @type cell :: atom() | number() | String.t()
  @type row :: %{optional(column()) => cell()}

  @spec tabs([row()], [column()], String.t()) :: Kino.Layout.t()
  @spec tabs([row()], [column()], String.t(), String.t() | nil) :: Kino.Layout.t()
  def tabs(rows, columns, filename, markdown_source \\ nil) do
    markdown_source = markdown_source || markdown(rows, columns)
    csv_source = csv(rows, columns)

    Kino.Layout.tabs([
      {"Interactive", Kino.DataTable.new(rows, keys: columns)},
      {"Markdown", Kino.Markdown.new(markdown_source)},
      {"CSV",
       Kino.Layout.grid([
         Kino.Download.new(fn -> csv_source end, filename: filename, label: "Download CSV"),
         Kino.Text.new(csv_source)
       ])}
    ])
  end

  @spec markdown([row()], [column()]) :: String.t()
  defp markdown(rows, columns) do
    header = markdown_row(columns)
    separator = markdown_row(Enum.map(columns, fn _ -> "---" end))

    body =
      Enum.map(rows, fn row ->
        markdown_row(Enum.map(columns, &Map.fetch!(row, &1)))
      end)

    Enum.join([header, separator | body], "\n") <> "\n"
  end

  @spec markdown_row([cell()]) :: String.t()
  defp markdown_row(values) do
    "| " <> Enum.map_join(values, " | ", &markdown_cell/1) <> " |"
  end

  @spec markdown_cell(cell()) :: String.t()
  defp markdown_cell(value) do
    value
    |> to_string()
    |> String.replace("\\", "\\\\")
    |> String.replace("|", "\\|")
    |> String.replace("\r\n", "<br>")
    |> String.replace(["\r", "\n"], "<br>")
  end

  @spec csv([row()], [column()]) :: String.t()
  defp csv(rows, columns) do
    records = [columns | Enum.map(rows, fn row -> Enum.map(columns, &Map.fetch!(row, &1)) end)]

    Enum.map_join(records, "\r\n", fn record ->
      Enum.map_join(record, ",", &csv_field/1)
    end) <> "\r\n"
  end

  @spec csv_field(cell()) :: String.t()
  defp csv_field(value) do
    "\"" <> String.replace(to_string(value), "\"", "\"\"") <> "\""
  end
end
```

## Reader's guide

**Neuroevolution through Elixir**  
Part I - Foundations

**The central idea:** represent possible solutions, generate variations, measure
their consequences, and decide what survives or reproduces. The representation
and operators determine which possibilities the search can reach.

This chapter remasters Gene I. Sher's *Handbook of Neuroevolution Through Erlang*
(2013), Chapter 3, printed pp. 81-104. The source is Chapter 3 of the complete
book in your Library. Original section numbers, examples, and conceptual order
are retained. Source notes refer to the chapter as **[S]**.

All Elixir/Nx code, executable experiments, numerical settings, new diagrams, and
the Generation-Evaluation-Selection (**GES**) interfaces are **remaster additions**.
Where an experiment changes a source example, the change is stated explicitly.
This is a study adaptation, not an official revised edition.

### Chapter map

| Section                                               | Question                                                    | Main representation                             |
| ----------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |
| 3.1 Evolution                                         | What does the biological narrative contribute?              | Prose and concept table                         |
