| 3.3 Formulating a Given Problem in Evolutionary Terms | How do we turn a task into a search?                        | Expression trees, data table, plot              |
| 3.4 The Different Flavors of Evolutionary Algorithms  | Which design choices distinguish the families?              | Comparison table                                |
| 3.4.1 Genetic Algorithms                              | How do crossover and mutation change encoded candidates?    | A complete batched camouflage search            |
| 3.4.2 Genetic Programming                             | How do we vary programs instead of bit strings?             | Tree operators and invariants                   |
| 3.4.3 Evolutionary Strategies                         | Can variation settings themselves be inherited and changed? | Self-adaptive mutation example                  |
| 3.4.4 Evolutionary Programming                        | What changes when the genome is a state-transition table?   | A finite-state predictor                        |
| 3.5 A Few Words on Memetic Computing                  | Why tune a design before judging it?                        | Global family choice and local parameter search |
